    "body": "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Quickstart | Acme Hooks</title><link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/markdown\" href=\"https://acme.example/docs/quickstart.md\"></head><body>\n<h1>Quickstart</h1>\n<p>Acme Hooks posts to your app when something happens. Install the CLI, sign in, create a hook.</p>\n<h2>Install</h2>\n<pre><code>npx -y https://acme.example/dl/acme-cli.tgz init\n</code></pre>\n<p>Then read <a href=\"https://acme.example/docs/install\">the install guide</a> and <a href=\"https://acme.example/docs/auth\">how sign-in works</a>; pricing is at <a href=\"https://acme.example/pricing\">pricing</a>.</p>\n<h2>Call the API</h2>\n<pre><code>curl -X POST https://acme.example/api/v1/hooks \\\n  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $ACME_API_KEY&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  -d &#39;{&quot;hook&quot;:&quot;orders&quot;}&#39;\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code>const response = await fetch(&quot;https://acme.example/api/v1/hooks&quot;, {\n  method: &quot;POST&quot;,\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.ACME_API_KEY}`,\n    &quot;Content-Type&quot;: &quot;application/json&quot;,\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({ hook: &quot;orders&quot; }),\n});\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Connect the MCP server</h2>\n<p>Add <code>https://acme.example/mcp</code> to your coding agent. The server lists your hooks and can create one.</p>\n<p>Markdown twin: <a href=\"https://acme.example/docs/quickstart.md\">quickstart.md</a>. Sign up at <a href=\"https://acme.example/signup\">signup</a>.</p>\n</body></html>\n"
